---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Newsletter privacy — styleguide.fyi" description="What the styleguide.fyi newsletter signup stores, how the launch list works, and how to remove your email address." canonicalPath="/privacy" markdownUrl={null} analytics={false}>
	<article class="privacy-page"><h1>Your email, for the newsletter.</h1><p>Updated October 17, 2026.</p><h2>What signing up does</h2><p>The form adds your email address to the styleguide.fyi newsletter launch list. Email delivery has not launched. Signing up does not send a confirmation email or verify that you own the address.</p><h2>What we store</h2><p>We store your email address, signup time, the version of the consent wording you accepted, and a protected value for your private unsubscribe link in a Cloudflare D1 database. The signup handler does not save your IP address or log the submitted email. Cloudflare processes requests to host the site and limit abusive submissions.</p><p>The list is private. There is no public subscriber directory or export endpoint. We use it to prepare the styleguide.fyi newsletter, not to sell email addresses. Unverified launch signups must be confirmed before regular newsletter delivery begins.</p><h2>Removing your address</h2><p>After signing up, save the private unsubscribe link shown with the confirmation. Opening it presents a removal button; confirming removes that signup from the active database. Cloudflare backup retention may temporarily preserve previous database states.</p><p>If you already signed up, use your original private link. Submitting an address again does not reveal its existing link or create another subscription. If you lose the link, contact the maintainer through the <a href="https://github.com/steventsao/styleguidefyi">repository profile</a>; do not post your email address in a public issue.</p><h2>Site analytics</h2><p>The reading pages use PostHog when configured. Newsletter forms are excluded from automatic capture, and input values are masked. The newsletter, unsubscribe, and privacy pages do not load analytics. Unsubscribe tokens stay in the URL fragment, which is not sent with a page request.</p><p><a href="/newsletter">Back to the newsletter</a> · <a href="/blog">Read the blog</a></p></article>
</Base>
<style>
	.privacy-page { max-width: 72ch; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 24px 0; }
	h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
	h2 { margin-top: 40px; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
	p { color: var(--text-secondary); }
</style>
